 "boundary": "from each routine entry state to NEWOPS with LOC outside the file, an exit of the interpreter bodies (lm: POODOO1, ALARM1; cm: POODOO, ALARM), or a transfer to an outside basic routine (cm: 2PHSCHNG, 6711, ALARM, BANKCALL, CHANG2, CHECKMM, DOWNFLAG, ENDMARK, ENDOFJOB, FALTON, FINDVAC, FLASHOFF, GENTRAN, IBNKCALL, NOVAC, NVSUB, NXTBNK, PHASCHNG, POODOO, POSTJUMP, PRIOCHNG, Q+1, RTB PINBRNCH, SELFCHK, STOPRATE, STSHOSUM, TASKOVER, TPAGREE, TRFAILOF, UPFLAG, V70UPDAT, V71UPDAT, V72UPDAT, V73UPDAT, WAITLIST, idle point); whole-file basic code stops at any transfer from the file to a fixed address outside it but INTPRET (stored words the file transfers to in erasable run on)",
 "compared": "Z, 2048 erasable words (A, L 16-bit) and the interrupt-enable state, the I/O channels 07, 12, 30 and the 31A/31B/32 trap flags",
